  "note": "Detector-calibration POSITIVES: two held-out questions per forget10 author, question offsets 15 and 17, disjoint as items from the exclusion, engineering, discovery and smoke cohorts. These share AUTHORS with the forget-policy cohort by construction and cannot do otherwise: the detector's prototypes are those authors, so a positive about a different author would not be a positive. Author-level held-out positives need a new unlearning checkpoint over a fresh concept split. Recall measured here is therefore held out at the QUESTION level only, and the calibration artefact says so.",
